WEBVTT

00:00.960 --> 00:04.980
Line AC is tangent to
circle O at point C.

00:04.980 --> 00:09.950
So this is line AC, tangent
to circle O at point

00:09.950 --> 00:13.640
C. What is the
length of segment AC?

00:13.640 --> 00:16.850
What is this distance right over
here, between point A and point

00:16.850 --> 00:17.350
C?

00:17.350 --> 00:19.550
And I encourage you
now to pause this video

00:19.550 --> 00:22.290
and try this out on your own.

00:22.290 --> 00:24.500
So I'm assuming you've
given a go at it.

00:24.500 --> 00:26.580
So the key thing
to realize here,

00:26.580 --> 00:31.280
since AC is tangent to the
circle at point C, that

00:31.280 --> 00:33.770
means it's going to be
perpendicular to the radius

00:33.770 --> 00:36.710
between the center of
the circle and point C.

00:36.710 --> 00:40.480
So this right over
here is a right angle.

00:40.480 --> 00:42.700
And the reason
why that is useful

00:42.700 --> 00:47.660
is now we know that triangle
AOC is a right triangle.

00:47.660 --> 00:49.576
So if we know two
of its sides, we

00:49.576 --> 00:50.950
could use the
Pythagorean theorem

00:50.950 --> 00:52.660
to figure out the third.

00:52.660 --> 00:55.260
Now, we clearly know OC.

00:55.260 --> 00:57.700
Now OA, we don't
know the entire side.

00:57.700 --> 01:00.760
They only give us
that AB is equal to 2.

01:00.760 --> 01:03.410
But the thing that might
jump out in your mind

01:03.410 --> 01:06.820
is OB is a radius.

01:06.820 --> 01:09.190
It's going to be the same
length as any radius.

01:09.190 --> 01:10.967
So this is going
to be 3 as well.

01:10.967 --> 01:13.050
It's the distance between
the center of the circle

01:13.050 --> 01:15.920
and a point on the circle, just
like the distance between O

01:15.920 --> 01:18.300
and C. So this is
going to be 3 as well.

01:18.300 --> 01:20.220
And so now we are
able to figure out

01:20.220 --> 01:26.760
that the hypotenuse of
this triangle has length 5.

01:26.760 --> 01:31.620
And so we need to figure out
what the length of segment AC

01:31.620 --> 01:32.190
is.

01:32.190 --> 01:33.773
So let's just call
that, I don't know.

01:33.773 --> 01:38.470
I'll call that x.

01:38.470 --> 01:42.430
And so we know that x
squared plus 3 squared--

01:42.430 --> 01:46.340
I'm just applying the
Pythagorean theorem here--

01:46.340 --> 01:48.800
is going to be equal to the
length of the hypotenuse

01:48.800 --> 01:52.594
squared, is going to
be equal to 5 squared.

01:52.594 --> 01:54.010
And I know this
is the hypotenuse.

01:54.010 --> 01:56.090
It's the side opposite
the 90-degree angle.

01:56.090 --> 01:59.530
It's the longest side
of the right triangle.

01:59.530 --> 02:09.650
So x squared plus
9 is equal to 25.

02:09.650 --> 02:13.900
Subtract 9 from
both sides, and you

02:13.900 --> 02:18.020
get x squared is equal to 16.

02:18.020 --> 02:19.940
And so it should jump
out at you that x

02:19.940 --> 02:23.810
is going to be equal to 4.

02:23.810 --> 02:25.440
So x is equal to 4.

02:25.440 --> 02:29.860
x is the same thing as
the length of segment AC,

02:29.860 --> 02:32.657
so the length of
segment AC is 4.
